          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Nikki directly avows love as a present emotional state. The narration explicitly characterizes the utterance as an honest admission, making truth-state presentation its dominant force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty that left them both vulnerable but deeply connected.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The expression does not itself undertake a promise, obligation, defined relationship, or future course of action. Keith reciprocates the avowal, but neither utterance establishes explicit commitment terms.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"“I love you,” she said suddenly, the words spilling out before she could stop them.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"“I love you too,” he said, his voice steady and sincere.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"Although the expression is principally an avowal, its sudden, uncontrolled production and characterization as a release substantially support affective discharge beyond merely emotional delivery.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"She turned to him, her heart full. “I love you,” she said suddenly, the words spilling out before she could stop them.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"No core function outside avowal and affective release is evidenced. In particular, the target is not framed as a request, command, apology, or other distinct act.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After an intimate encounter, Nikki and Keith are lying in bed. With her heart described as full, Nikki suddenly tells Keith that she loves him; Keith pauses, smiles, and reciprocates. The narration presents the exchange as honest, vulnerable, and connecting.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Nikki undertakes no explicit obligation or future action in the target expression. Keith accepts and reciprocates the emotional avowal by saying that he loves her too, but this is uptake of the admission rather than acceptance of a specified commitment.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the supplied passage as a particular work.\",\"limitations\":\"The supplied passage strongly supports Nikki's affection at this moment, but it does not establish precise relationship terms or any promise arising from the target expression.\"}"
        }
